# Independent 3D hydro crosscheck

`x3i_wind.cpp` is our problem generator for a pinned, external Athena++
dependency. It shares the observational parser/physical units with the
in-house solver; fluxes, spherical geometry, integration and gravity are
independent Athena implementations. No production CPU solver was modified.

The calculation uses spherical axes `(r,theta,phi)`, periodic longitude,
open latitude/outer boundaries, gamma 1.5, solar gravity and
`p=2 n_p k_B T`. Absolute simulation time is days since 2025-11-01 UTC.
Scalar calibration, map phase and probe coordinates match `results/hydro`.
Constant supersonic inner ghost states yield exactly the prescribed inner
mass flux; this is audited at every step. Probes interpolate Cartesian
conserved variables in space/time using the same convention as the baseline.

`prepare.py` records the source/patch/input provenance and prepares the
external dependency; `run.py build`, `run.py pilot`, and `run.py hydro`
build and execute serially with finite wall/CPU/memory limits. The 0.1-day
pilot precedes the 25-day run. Native binary VTK, compatible final NumPy
arrays, probe CSVs, logs and measured resource statistics are preserved.
`frozen_inputs` contains content-identical copies of the original forcing
and probe files; completed run configs retain their actual original paths,
whose checksums are recorded in `provenance.json`.

The saved `strict_floors.patch` inserts a hard error before every upstream
hydro density/pressure floor. It changes no valid state or numerical flux.
All runs completed with positive states and no floor activation. The coarse
run used about 67 MB RSS and 4.38 s wall time on one thread.

| Method/grid | PN-weighted incident proton flux (cm^-2 s^-1) |
|---|---:|
| Baseline hydro, 48×4×48 | 1.51106e8 |
| Local-LLF hydro, 48×4×48 | 2.00225e8 |
| Independent Athena HLLC, 48×4×48 | 1.12276e8 |
| Independent Athena HLLC, 72×8×72 | 1.44362e8 |
| Independent Athena HLLC, 96×12×96 | 1.29244e8 |

The large numerical-method sensitivity exists with B=0 and therefore cannot
be attributed solely to magnetic cleaning. The independent hydro model is
itself not density/flux converged: its 72→96 mean incident change is −10.47%,
and time-local differences reach 24.48%, despite speed differences below
1.9%. The comparisons are controls, not evidence that one forecast is true.
`comparison.json`, `local_llf_vs_baseline.json`, `athena_vs_local_llf.json`,
`medium_vs_coarse.json`, and `fine_vs_medium.json` retain both PN-only and
all-detector GTI conventions explicitly.

`radial_audit.py` independently solves the steady supersonic polytropic
Bernoulli/mass-flux equations for a uniform 1.8 MK inner wind with gravity.
The saved hot controls show baseline coarse speed/density errors of
−2.47%/+2.57% and Athena errors −0.352%/+0.121%; both conserve radial mass
flux to about 0.3%. Thus a large pressure/unit/gravity mismatch does not
explain the much larger time-dependent stream differences. This test
strengthens, rather than replaces, the original cold radial geometry test.
// Own solar-wind problem generator for the independent Athena++ dependency.
// The observation parser/units are shared; numerical flux, geometry, integration
// and gravity are Athena++ implementations. This generator is HYDRO only.
#include <memory>
#include <stdexcept>
#include "../athena.hpp"
#include "../athena_arrays.hpp"
#include "../bvals/bvals.hpp"
#include "../coordinates/coordinates.hpp"
#include "../eos/eos.hpp"
#include "../hydro/hydro.hpp"
#include "../mesh/mesh.hpp"
#include "../parameter_input.hpp"
#include "x3i_boundary.hpp"

#if MAGNETIC_FIELDS_ENABLED
#error "x3i_wind is an independent hydrodynamic control; do not enable magnetic fields"
#endif

namespace {
using State=std::array<double,5>;
using x3i::V;
using x3i::dot;
using x3i::mul;
using x3i::add;
std::unique_ptr<x3i::Config> cfg;
std::unique_ptr<x3i::Boundary> boundary;
double gamma_gas, rmin, previous_day, minimum_density=1e99,minimum_pressure=1e99;
double maximum_inner_mass_flux_error=0, minimum_inflow_mach=1e99;
int nr, nt, np;
std::vector<double> radii,thetas,phis;
std::vector<State> previous;
struct Probe {double day,r,lon,lat;int id;};
std::vector<Probe> probes;
size_t next_probe=0;
std::ofstream probe_out;
std::filesystem::path output;

V er(double t,double p){return {std::sin(t)*std::cos(p),std::sin(t)*std::sin(p),std::cos(t)};}
V et(double t,double p){return {std::cos(t)*std::cos(p),std::cos(t)*std::sin(p),-std::sin(t)};}
V ep(double p){return {-std::sin(p),std::cos(p),0};}
size_t index(int i,int j,int k){return ((size_t)i*nt+j)*np+k;}

// Return density, radial/polar/azimuthal velocity, pressure in solver units.
State analytic(double day,double radius,double theta,double phi,bool retard) {
  double lag=retard?(radius-rmin)/((boundary->speed+boundary->speed_offset)*1000/x3i::VUNIT):0;
  auto b=boundary->sample(day-lag,phi,x3i::X3IPI/2-theta);
  double density=b[1]/(radius*radius), v=b[0]*1000/x3i::VUNIT;
  double temperature=b[3]*std::pow(radius/rmin,-2*(gamma_gas-1));
  double pressure=cfg->d("thermal_pressure_factor",2)*density*1e6*x3i::KB*temperature/x3i::PUNIT;
  double vp=cfg->d("boundary_vphi_kms",0)*1000/x3i::VUNIT*rmin/radius;
  return {density,v,0,vp,pressure};
}

void inner(MeshBlock*,Coordinates*co,AthenaArray<Real>&w,FaceField&,Real day,Real,
           int il,int,int jl,int ju,int kl,int ku,int ngh) {
  for(int k=kl;k<=ku;++k)for(int j=jl;j<=ju;++j){
    State z=analytic(day,rmin,co->x2v(j),co->x3v(k),false);
    // Constant ghost states make the left PLM interface state exactly equal to
    // the imposed face state. For supersonic HLLC inflow its physical flux is
    // therefore the same prescribed flux as the in-house hydro calculation.
    for(int i=il-ngh;i<il;++i){w(IDN,k,j,i)=z[0];w(IVX,k,j,i)=z[1];
      w(IVY,k,j,i)=z[2];w(IVZ,k,j,i)=z[3];w(IPR,k,j,i)=z[4];}
  }
}

std::vector<State> capture(MeshBlock* block) {
  std::vector<State> states((size_t)nr*nt*np);
  auto&u=block->phydro->u;
  for(int i=0;i<nr;++i)for(int j=0;j<nt;++j)for(int k=0;k<np;++k){
    int ii=i+block->is,jj=j+block->js,kk=k+block->ks;
    V e=er(thetas[j],phis[k]),t=et(thetas[j],phis[k]),p=ep(phis[k]);
    V momentum=add(add(mul(e,u(IM1,kk,jj,ii)),mul(t,u(IM2,kk,jj,ii))),mul(p,u(IM3,kk,jj,ii)));
    State z={u(IDN,kk,jj,ii),momentum[0],momentum[1],momentum[2],u(IEN,kk,jj,ii)};
    double pressure=(gamma_gas-1)*(z[4]-.5*(z[1]*z[1]+z[2]*z[2]+z[3]*z[3])/z[0]);
    if(!(z[0]>1e-15&&pressure>1e-15&&std::isfinite(pressure)))
      throw std::runtime_error("Independent hydro state became nonphysical or approached its configured floor");
    minimum_density=std::min(minimum_density,z[0]);minimum_pressure=std::min(minimum_pressure,pressure);
    states[index(i,j,k)]=z;
  }
  return states;
}

State sample(const std::vector<State>&s,const Probe&q) {
  auto bracket=[](const std::vector<double>&v,double x){
    if(x<v.front()-1e-10||x>v.back()+1e-10)throw std::runtime_error("Probe outside cell-center interpolation domain");
    int i=std::clamp(int(std::upper_bound(v.begin(),v.end(),x)-v.begin())-1,0,int(v.size())-2);
    return std::pair<int,double>{i,(x-v[i])/(v[i+1]-v[i])};};
  auto [i,fi]=bracket(radii,q.r);auto[j,fj]=bracket(thetas,x3i::X3IPI/2-q.lat);
  double kp=x3i::wrap(q.lon)/(2*x3i::X3IPI/np)-.5;int k=std::floor(kp);double fk=kp-k;
  State z={};
  for(int di=0;di<2;++di)for(int dj=0;dj<2;++dj)for(int dk=0;dk<2;++dk){
    double w=(di?fi:1-fi)*(dj?fj:1-fj)*(dk?fk:1-fk);
    const State&a=s[index(i+di,j+dj,((k+dk)%np+np)%np)];
    for(int v=0;v<5;++v)z[v]+=w*a[v];
  }
  return z;
}

void write_probe(const Probe&q,const std::vector<State>&current,double current_day) {
  State left=sample(previous,q),right=sample(current,q),z;
  double f=current_day==previous_day?1:std::clamp((q.day-previous_day)/(current_day-previous_day),0.,1.);
  for(int v=0;v<5;++v)z[v]=(1-f)*left[v]+f*right[v];
  V vel={z[1]/z[0],z[2]/z[0],z[3]/z[0]};double speed=x3i::norm(vel)*x3i::VUNIT/1000;
  double pressure=(gamma_gas-1)*(z[4]-.5*z[0]*dot(vel,vel));
  V e=er(x3i::X3IPI/2-q.lat,q.lon),t=et(x3i::X3IPI/2-q.lat,q.lon),p=ep(q.lon);
  probe_out<<q.day<<','<<q.id<<','<<q.r<<','<<q.lon<<','<<q.lat<<','<<z[0]<<','<<speed<<','<<z[0]*speed*1e5
    <<','<<dot(vel,e)*x3i::VUNIT/1000<<','<<dot(vel,t)*x3i::VUNIT/1000<<','<<dot(vel,p)*x3i::VUNIT/1000
    <<','<<pressure*x3i::PUNIT*1e9<<",0,0,0\n";
}

void npy(const std::filesystem::path&path,const std::vector<float>&v,const std::vector<int>&shape){
  std::ofstream f(path,std::ios::binary);std::string h="{'descr': '<f4', 'fortran_order': False, 'shape': (";
  for(int n:shape)h+=std::to_string(n)+", ";h+="), }";while((10+h.size()+1)%64)h+=' ';h+='\n';
  f.write("\x93NUMPY\x01\x00",8);uint16_t size=h.size();f.put(size&255);f.put(size>>8);
  f.write(h.data(),h.size());f.write(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(v.data()),v.size()*sizeof(float));
  if(!f)throw std::runtime_error("Cannot save independent hydro snapshot");
}
}

void Mesh::InitUserMeshData(ParameterInput*pin) {
  cfg.reset(new x3i::Config(pin->GetString("problem","config_file")));
  boundary.reset(new x3i::Boundary(*cfg));gamma_gas=cfg->d("gamma",1.5);rmin=cfg->d("rmin_au",.1);
  if(std::abs(gamma_gas-pin->GetReal("hydro","gamma"))>1e-12)throw std::runtime_error("Gamma mismatch");
  output=pin->GetString("problem","output_dir");std::filesystem::create_directories(output);
  EnrollUserBoundaryFunction(BoundaryFace::inner_x1,inner);
  x3i::Csv csv(cfg->s("probes_csv"));int it=csv.col("day"),ir=csv.col("r_au"),ip=csv.col("lon_rad"),il=csv.col("lat_rad"),id=csv.col("probe_id",false);
  for(auto&z:csv.rows)probes.push_back({z[it],z[ir],z[ip],z[il],id<0?0:int(z[id])});
  std::sort(probes.begin(),probes.end(),[](const Probe&a,const Probe&b){return a.day<b.day;});
  while(next_probe<probes.size()&&probes[next_probe].day<start_time-1e-12)++next_probe;
  probe_out.open(output/"probe.csv");probe_out<<std::setprecision(12)
    <<"day,probe_id,r_au,lon_rad,lat_rad,n_cm3,speed_kms,flux_cm2_s,vr_kms,vtheta_kms,vphi_kms,p_npa,Br_nt,Btheta_nt,Bphi_nt\n";
}

void MeshBlock::ProblemGenerator(ParameterInput*) {
  if(pmy_mesh->nbtotal!=1)throw std::runtime_error("Independent hydro prototype requires a single serial MeshBlock");
  nr=ie-is+1;nt=je-js+1;np=ke-ks+1;radii.resize(nr);thetas.resize(nt);phis.resize(np);
  for(int i=0;i<nr;++i)radii[i]=pcoord->x1v(i+is);
  for(int j=0;j<nt;++j)thetas[j]=pcoord->x2v(j+js);
  for(int k=0;k<np;++k)phis[k]=pcoord->x3v(k+ks);
  for(int k=ks-NGHOST;k<=ke+NGHOST;++k)for(int j=js-NGHOST;j<=je+NGHOST;++j)for(int i=is-NGHOST;i<=ie+NGHOST;++i){
    double radius=std::max(rmin,double(pcoord->x1v(i)));
    State z=analytic(pmy_mesh->time,radius,pcoord->x2v(j),pcoord->x3v(k),radius>rmin);
    phydro->u(IDN,k,j,i)=z[0];phydro->u(IM1,k,j,i)=z[0]*z[1];phydro->u(IM2,k,j,i)=z[0]*z[2];
    phydro->u(IM3,k,j,i)=z[0]*z[3];phydro->u(IEN,k,j,i)=z[4]/(gamma_gas-1)+.5*z[0]*(z[1]*z[1]+z[2]*z[2]+z[3]*z[3]);
  }
  previous=capture(this);previous_day=pmy_mesh->time;
  while(next_probe<probes.size()&&probes[next_probe].day<=previous_day+1e-12)write_probe(probes[next_probe++],previous,previous_day);
}

void Mesh::UserWorkInLoop() {
  MeshBlock*block=my_blocks(0);auto current=capture(block);double current_day=time+dt;
  while(next_probe<probes.size()&&probes[next_probe].day<=current_day+1e-12)write_probe(probes[next_probe++],current,current_day);
  for(int k=block->ks;k<=block->ke;++k)for(int j=block->js;j<=block->je;++j){
    State expected=analytic(current_day,rmin,block->pcoord->x2v(j),block->pcoord->x3v(k),false);
    minimum_inflow_mach=std::min(minimum_inflow_mach,expected[1]/std::sqrt(gamma_gas*expected[4]/expected[0]));
    double f=block->phydro->flux[X1DIR](IDN,k,j,block->is),target=expected[0]*expected[1];
    maximum_inner_mass_flux_error=std::max(maximum_inner_mass_flux_error,std::abs(f-target)/std::abs(target));
  }
  previous.swap(current);previous_day=current_day;
}

